Move the base image from alpine 3.22 to alpine 3.23. Two properties of the new base are worth knowing about. unbound 1.24 logs `so-sndbuf 4194304 was not granted` at startup unless the host raises `net.core.wmem_max`; it falls back to the system default and keeps working, so the message is noise rather than a fault. And alpine decides per architecture whether rspamd is built against LuaJIT: amd64 and arm64 get it back on 3.23, `linux/arm/v7` does not, which is why the DMARC reporting workaround in `core/rspamd/Dockerfile` stays in place.
